        "original_id": "a0552e71-9811-5957-9ee1-c4d69780a69c",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Joseph E. Grosberg\n- Companies: Central Markets, Price Chopper Supermarkets\n- Places: Upstate New York, Downtown Schenectady, Nott Street\n- Topics: American supermarket industry, wholesale foods industry\n\nFacts:\n- Joseph E. Grosberg was born on December 27, 1883.\n- Joseph E. Grosberg was a pioneer in the American supermarket industry and wholesale foods industry.\n- Joseph E. Grosberg was a founder and president of Central Markets.\n- Central Markets was a chain of grocery stores in upstate New York that established some of the first supermarkets in the United States.\n- Central Markets is now known as Price Chopper Supermarkets.\n- Joseph E. Grosberg died on July 25, 1970.\n- On June 2, 2010, Price Chopper Supermarkets dedicated its new headquarters on Nott Street in Downtown Schenectady.",
